  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1222 PM CST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nThe mid and upper level pattern will become highly amplified next \nweek with an upper ridge over the Rockies and deep troughing over \nthe west coast and eastern US. A number of short wave perturbations \nwill rotate around the larger trough in the eastern US next week. \nThese short waves will have little affect on the weather locally \nwith the colder air remaining to the east of the area. Model \nguidance currently shows little chance of a freeze for the central \nSouth Plains through late next week. In fact, the AIGEFS shows only \na 6% probability of a freeze for Lubbock before Nov 23 which is the \nrecord date for latest first freeze.",
